.TH SENDTO 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sendto \- send bytes to a socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B ssize_t sendto(int descriptor, const void* buffer, size_t length, int flags,
.B                const struct sockaddr* address, socklen_t address_length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends bytes, optionally to a supplied destination address. On a connected
socket the address may be NULL. MSG_NOSIGNAL suppresses SIGPIPE for this call.
Sends can be short and are not retried.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes sent, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recvfrom (3crunch),
.BR sendto (2)
